TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Image 1"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Useful Links"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The text links ocean acidification to coral bleaching too directly. Marine heat stress is the main proximate cause of mass bleaching; acidification is a separate stressor that can impair coral calcification. The 30% figure is better described as an increase in hydrogen-ion concentration, not a general increase in ocean acidity."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"Near-real-time monitoring is asserted without specifying the sensor, revisit interval, latency, or communications design. If the concept relies on one low-Earth-orbit satellite, it would not provide continuous or near-real-time coverage of the reef; the requirement needs a coverage analysis or a multi-satellite/other architecture."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"No technical mission parameters or preliminary results are provided, such as a candidate orbit, coverage/revisit estimate, payload capability, or link analysis. The plan names these future tasks but does not yet demonstrate their feasibility."}],"overall":"Weighted result: 58/100 (using the criterion weights and marks out of 10). The mission rationale and project schedule are credible, but the report is light on defined requirements and contains no preliminary engineering results. Clarify the bleaching science and establish coverage and payload requirements to guide the full design.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":24.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"The report explains the reef-monitoring purpose, identifies scientific and conservation users, and gives a strong Australian rationale. The mission function and intended benefits are understandable, with relevant sources. However, it does not define a specific payload, measurable objectives, or operational requirements, so the concept is not yet complete enough for Accomplished.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Hundreds of millions of humans rely on reefs for food, natural protection, jobs, and tourism."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":18.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"A week-by-week Gantt chart is accompanied by descriptions of research, launch, orbit, ground control, communications, end-of-life, and STK work. A useful source list is included and the tasks appear feasible within the stated timeline. The plan lacks contingency provision, detailed deliverables or dependencies, and a clear explanation of why particular activities or sequencing suit this mission.","evidence":[{"where":"Image 1","quote":""},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"The goal is to brainstorm and research as many possible strategies for the satellite’s launch/orbit"},{"where":"Useful Links","quote":"https://coralreefwatch.noaa.gov/satellite/publications/nim_skirving_reef_vulnerability.pdf"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Relevant background research and STK tutorials show some work has been completed. However, the submission presents no preliminary technical design results, calculations, simulations, or interpretation. This fits minor progress rather than a good preliminary set of results.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"researched into how coral bleaching occurs and its severity"},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4"}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":12.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"The report has a clear section structure, a readable and labelled Gantt chart, and relevant sources are linked to numbered citations. The prose is generally understandable, but includes awkward or informal phrasing, and the references are mostly bare URLs without full bibliographic details. The chart also does not explain the meaning of its grey cells.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"where":"Image 1","quote":""},{"where":"Useful Links","quote":"Useful Links"}]}]}
